---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
const curl = `curl "https://api.barcodenest.com/v1/products/3017620422003" \\
  -H "X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY"`;
const success = `{
  "barcode": "3017620422003",
  "barcode_type": "EAN-13",
  "canonical_gtin": "03017620422003",
  "valid": true,
  "found": true,
  "product": {
    "name": "Nutella",
    "brand": "Ferrero",
    "categories": ["spreads", "hazelnut spreads"],
    "quantity": "400 g",
    "image_url": null,
    "ingredients": "Sugar, palm oil, hazelnuts, skimmed milk powder…",
    "allergens": ["milk", "nuts", "soybeans"],
    "nutrition": { "energy-kcal_100g": 539, "fat_100g": 30.9 },
    "countries": ["France", "Portugal"]
  },
  "source": {
    "name": "Open Food Facts",
    "source_id": "3017620422003"
  },
  "error": null
}`;
const batch = `curl -X POST "https://api.barcodenest.com/v1/products/batch" \\
  -H "X-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"barcodes":["3017620422003","4006381333931","123"]}'`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Barcode Lookup API Documentation | BarcodeNest" description="Integrate the BarcodeNest barcode API with curl examples, authentication, EAN and GTIN formats, response schemas, batch lookups, errors, and rate limits." current="docs">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">API documentation · v1</div><h1>Build your first barcode lookup.</h1><p class="lede">Everything you need to validate a barcode, retrieve a product, and handle production responses.</p></div></header>
  <div class="container docs-layout">
    <aside class="docs-nav" aria-label="Documentation sections">
      <strong>On this page</strong>
      <a href="#quick-start">Quick start</a><a href="#authentication">Authentication</a><a href="#account-api">Account API</a><a href="#single-lookup">Single barcode lookup</a><a href="#barcodes">Barcode formats</a><a href="#batch">Batch barcode lookup</a><a href="#errors">Errors</a><a href="#limits">Limits & headers</a>
    </aside>
    <div class="docs-content">
      <section id="quick-start"><h2>Quick start</h2><ol class="docs-steps"><li><span>1</span><div><strong>Register</strong><p><a href="/register">Create a Free account</a>. Your first API key is generated automatically.</p></div></li><li><span>2</span><div><strong>Login</strong><p>Registration signs you in automatically. Return through <a href="/login/">Login</a> whenever needed.</p></div></li><li><span>3</span><div><strong>Copy API Key</strong><p>Copy the key from onboarding and store it securely. The full value is shown once.</p></div></li><li><span>4</span><div><strong>Make your first request</strong><p>Send the key in the <code class="inline-code">X-API-Key</code> header.</p></div></li></ol><p>All version 1 API requests use <code class="inline-code">https://api.barcodenest.com</code>.</p><CodeBlock label="First request" code={curl} language="bash" /></section>
      <section id="authentication"><h2>Authentication</h2><p>Send your API key in the <code class="inline-code">X-API-Key</code> request header. Do not expose one in client-side code or public repositories.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Need a key?</strong> <a href="/register"><u>Create a Free account</u></a> to receive one immediately.</div></section>
      <section id="account-api"><h2>Account authentication</h2><p>Register with email and password, Google, or GitHub. Social sign-in uses the provider-confirmed identity without a separate BarcodeNest email-verification step. Account endpoints use short-lived JWT Bearer tokens. Browser sessions use Secure, HttpOnly cookies and rotating refresh tokens; developer API keys remain the credential for product lookups.</p><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /v1/auth/login</code></td><td>Authenticate with email and password.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/auth/oauth/google</code></td><td>Begin Google sign-in.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/auth/oauth/github</code></td><td>Begin GitHub sign-in.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /v1/auth/refresh</code></td><td>Rotate a refresh token and issue a new token pair.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /v1/auth/logout</code></td><td>Revoke the server-side session.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/account</code></td><td>Read the authenticated account.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET/POST /v1/account/api-keys</code></td><td>List keys or create a key that is shown once.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/account/usage</code></td><td>Read current monthly usage and remaining quota.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
      <section id="single-lookup"><h2>Single barcode lookup</h2><p><code class="inline-code">GET /v1/products/&#123;barcode&#125;</code></p><p>The endpoint validates the submitted code, resolves its canonical GTIN-14 identity, and returns the indexed product when found.</p><CodeBlock label="200 response" code={success} language="json" /><p>Fields can be <code class="inline-code">null</code> or empty when the source record does not contain them. Product field availability is not guaranteed.</p></section>
      <section id="barcodes"><h2>Barcode formats</h2><p>The current implementation accepts ASCII digits with a valid check digit in these lengths:</p><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Length</th><th>Canonical behaviour</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>EAN-8</td><td>8</td><td>Zero-padded to GTIN-14</td></tr><tr><td>UPC-A</td><td>12</td><td>Zero-padded to GTIN-14</td></tr><tr><td>EAN-13</td><td>13</td><td>Zero-padded to GTIN-14</td></tr><tr><td>GTIN-14</td><td>14</td><td>Used as supplied</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Equivalent UPC, EAN and GTIN-14 representations are matched to the same canonical identity where applicable. BarcodeNest currently documents EAN-8, EAN-13 and GTIN-14 as primary formats; UPC-A is also accepted by the API.</p></section>
      <section id="batch"><h2>Batch barcode lookup</h2><p><code class="inline-code">POST /v1/products/batch</code></p><p>Submit up to 100 barcodes. A mixed batch returns <code class="inline-code">200</code> with one result per input; invalid or unknown items do not fail the whole request.</p><CodeBlock label="Batch request" code={batch} language="bash" /><p>Each successful batch request consumes one monthly API call and counts as one request against the per-minute request rate.</p></section>
      <section id="errors"><h2>Errors</h2><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Code / behaviour</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td class="status">200</td><td>Found, or batch completed</td><td>A single barcode lookup found a record; batches can contain found, unknown, and invalid results.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="status">400</td><td><code>invalid_barcode</code></td><td>The barcode lookup input is non-numeric, has an unsupported length, or fails its check digit.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="status">401</td><td><code>missing_api_key</code>, <code>invalid_api_key</code>, <code>revoked_api_key</code>, or <code>expired_api_key</code></td><td>The API key cannot authenticate the request.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="status">404</td><td><code>product_not_found</code></td><td>The single barcode is valid, but no product is indexed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="status">422</td><td><code>empty_batch</code>, <code>batch_limit_exceeded</code>, or <code>request_validation_error</code></td><td>The batch body is empty, contains more than 100 items, or is structurally invalid.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="status">429</td><td><code>rate_limit_exceeded</code> or <code>usage_limit_reached</code></td><td>A per-minute request limit or monthly barcode lookup quota was exceeded.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></section>
      <section id="limits"><h2>Rate limits, quotas & headers</h2><p>Successful lookup responses include:</p><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Header</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code></td><td>Requests allowed per rolling 60-second window.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code></td><td>Requests remaining in that window.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-RateLimit-Reset</code></td><td>Unix timestamp when capacity begins to return.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-Monthly-Quota-Limit</code></td><td>Barcode lookups allowed in the current month.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-Monthly-Quota-Remaining</code></td><td>Barcode lookups remaining.</td></tr><tr><td><code>X-Monthly-Quota-Period</code></td><td>Quota period start date, for example <code>2026-07-01</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A rate-limit response also includes <code class="inline-code">Retry-After</code>. Monthly quota errors return the monthly quota headers.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
